<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">24 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 24 February, from 1525 to 1946.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pavia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-pavia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1525 CE <span class="tih-ago">501 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Imperial army captures Francis I at the Battle of Pavia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles V's troops routed the French outside Pavia, and King Francis I was taken prisoner. He was released in 1526 only after signing away claims in Italy and Burgundy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pavia">Battle of Pavia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1582 CE <span class="tih-ago">444 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Gregory XIII issues the bull reforming the calendar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The bull Inter gravissimas introduced the Gregorian calendar, dropping ten days that October to realign the calendar with the equinox. It is now the world's standard civil calendar.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1803 CE <span class="tih-ago">223 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marbury v. Madison establishes judicial review</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Chief Justice John Marshall ruled that the Supreme Court could strike down acts of Congress that conflicted with the Constitution. The decision became a cornerstone of American constitutional law.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1821 CE <span class="tih-ago">205 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Plan of Iguala sets out Mexican independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Agustín de Iturbide and Vicente Guerrero proclaimed a plan for an independent Mexican monarchy guaranteeing Catholicism and equality. Mexico's independence was declared that September.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1920 CE <span class="tih-ago">106 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hitler presents the Nazi Party's 25-point programme</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Hofbräuhaus in Munich, Hitler read out the programme of the German Workers' Party, which renamed itself the National Socialist German Workers' Party (NSDAP) around this time.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1946 CE <span class="tih-ago">80 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Juan Perón elected President of Argentina</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The former labour minister won the presidency with strong support from trade unions. With his wife Eva, he built the populist Peronist movement that still shapes Argentine politics.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a></div></div></li></ol>
